# Dashboard Hydration & Interactive Widgets

## Client Island Isolation
- Keep interactive islands atomic. Isolate interactive state (e.g., date pickers, real-time charts, filter dropdowns) to the smallest possible client component.
- Use the correct `client:` directive based on component necessity:
  - `client:visible`: Interactive charts or heavy data tables located below the primary fold.
  - `client:idle`: Non-critical background widgets, secondary analytics filters.
  - `client:load`: Primary date-range filter or global dashboard control bar (only if immediate interactivity is needed).

## Chart & Data Heavy Utilities
- Heavy charting libraries (Chart.js, Recharts, ECharts) MUST be lazy-loaded or hydrated with `client:visible`.
- Provide zero-layout-shift (CLS) skeletal placeholders while client charts load:

```astro
---
import InteractiveChart from '@/components/dashboard/InteractiveChart.tsx';
import ChartSkeleton from '@/components/dashboard/ChartSkeleton.astro';
---

<div class="relative min-h-[300px]">
  <InteractiveChart client:visible data="{Astro.props.chartData}">
    <!-- Astro fallback slotted content rendered server-side before hydration -->
    <ChartSkeleton slot="fallback"/>
  </InteractiveChart>
</div>